//! Host-independent port of Pi 1.3.0's *pure* compaction preparation, automatic
//! trigger and branch-collection decisions.
//!
//! The host's own [`crate::compaction`] modules operate on the host `Entry`/message
//! enums, which predate Pi 1.3.0's `context_edit` entries and projection model.
//! This module instead works directly on Pi-shaped JSON (`serde_json::Value`) so the
//! decision functions can be compared value-for-value against fixtures generated by
//! driving the *unchanged* upstream modules. See
//! `docs/provider-parity/check-compaction-pure-reference.mjs` and
//! `docs/provider-parity/check-compaction-trigger-reference.mjs`.
//!
//! Ported units:
//! - [`projection`]: `buildSessionPath`, `getSessionContextSettings`,
//!   `sessionEntryToContextMessages`, `buildContextEntries`, `projectContextEntry`,
//!   `buildSessionProjection`.
//! - [`tokens`]: `estimateTokens`, `calculateContextTokens`, `estimateContextTokens`,
//!   `estimateProjectedContextTokens`, `getCurrentSystemMessage` (transcript replay).
//! - [`file_ops`]: `extractFileOpsFromMessage`, `computeFileLists`,
//!   `formatFileOperations`.
//! - [`prepare`]: `findProjectedCutPoint`, `prepareCompaction`,
//!   `getSummarizationFailure`, `extractFileOperations`.
//! - [`branch`]: `collectEntriesForBranchSummary`, `prepareBranchEntries`.
//! - [`trigger`]: `isContextOverflow`, `isRecoverableLength`, `shouldCompact`, the
//!   `_checkCompaction` decision table.
//! - [`lifecycle`]: the `_runAutoCompaction` ordered operation model.
//!
//! JavaScript semantics are preserved deliberately: string lengths count UTF-16 code
//! units, `JSON.stringify` is reproduced for tool-call arguments, `||` fallbacks are
//! not replaced by null-coalescing, and sets keep insertion order. Numbers are
//! compared by value (JS `0` == Rust `0.0`) by [`json_eq`], the one blanket
//! normalization allowed by the lane contract.

